             "Cooling Properties of Cloudy Bag Strange Stars", "comments" -> 
             "23 pages, 14 figures, accepted by Astroparticle Physics, \
abstract\n  appeared here has been shortened", "journal-ref" -> 
             "Astropart.Phys.19:171-192,2003", "doi" -> 
             "10.1016/S0927-6505(02)00197-4", "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "astro-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  As the chiral symmetry is widely recognized as an important \
driver of the\nstrong interaction dynamics, current strange stars models \
based on MIT bag\nmodels do not obey such symmetry. We investigate properties \
of bare strange\nstars using the Cloudy Bag Model, in which a pion cloud \
coupled to the\nquark-confining bag is introduced such that chiral symmetry \
is conserved. We\nfind that in this model the decay of pions is a very \
efficient cooling way. In\nfact it can carry out most the thermal energy in a \
few milliseconds and\ndirectly convert them into 100MeV photons via pion \
decay. This may be a very\nefficient $\\gamma$-ray burst mechanism. \
Furthermore, the cooling behavior may\nprovide a possible way to distinguish \
a compact object between a neutron star,\nMIT strange star and Cloudy Bag \
strange star in observations.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Mon, 2 Sep 2002 08:03:23 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2008-11-26", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ng", "C. Y.", ""}, {
               "Cheng", "K. S.", ""}, {"Chu", "M. C.", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], 
