           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"0802.0783\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"S\\\\'ergio Sousa\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"S. G. Sousa and M. S. Cunha\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"On mode conversion and wave reflection in magnetic Ap \
stars\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"13 pages, 12 figures, accepted for publication in \
MNRAS\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1111/j.1365-2966.2008.13062.x\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We investigate the effect of a strong large scale \
magnetic field on the\\nreflection of high frequency acoustic modes in \
rapidly oscillating Ap stars. To\\nthat end we consider a toy model composed \
of an isothermal atmosphere matched\\nonto a polytropic interior and \
determine the numerical solution to the set of\\nideal magneto-hydrodynamic \
equations in a local plane-parallel approximation\\nwith constant gravity. \
Using the numerical solution in combination with\\napproximate analytical \
solutions that are valid in the limits where the\\nmagnetic and acoustic \
components are decoupled, we calculate the relative\\nfraction of energy flux \
that is carried away in each oscillation cycle by\\nrunning acoustic waves in \
the atmosphere and running magnetic waves in the\\ninterior. For oscillation \
frequencies above the acoustic cutoff we show that\\nmost energy losses \
associated with the presence of running waves occur in\\nregions where the \
magnetic field is close to vertical. Moreover, by considering\\nthe depth \
dependence of the energy associated with the magnetic component of\\nthe wave \
in the atmosphere we show that a fraction of the wave energy is kept\\nin the \
oscillation every cycle. For frequencies above the acoustic \
cutoff\\nfrequency such energy is concentrated in regions where the magnetic \
field is\\nsignificantly inclined in relation to the local vertical. Even \
though our\\ncalculations were aimed at studying oscillations with \
frequencies above the\\nacoustic cutoff frequency, based on our results we \
discuss what results may be\\nexpected for oscillations of lower \
frequency.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 6 Feb 2008 13:03:58 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
