                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  
                  "\"  We study the role of the Standard Model Higgs \
condensate, formed during\\ncosmological inflation, in the epoch of reheating \
that follows. We focus on the\\nscenario where the inflaton decays slowly and \
perturbatively, so that there is\\na long period between the end of inflation \
and the beginning of radiation\\ndomination. The Higgs condensate decays \
non-perturbatively during this period,\\nand we show that it heats the \
primordial plasma to much higher temperatures\\nthan would result from the \
slowly-decaying inflaton alone. We discuss the\\neffect of this hot plasma on \
the thermalization of the inflaton's decay\\nproducts, and study its \
phenomenological implications for the formation of\\ncosmological relics like \
dark matter, with associated isocurvature\\nfluctuations, and the restoration \
of the electroweak and Peccei-Quinn\\nsymmetries.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
