             "  Penrose's identification with warp provides the general \
framework for\nconstructing the continuous form of impulsive gravitational \
wave metrics. We\npresent the 2-component spinor formalism for the derivation \
of the full family\nof impulsive spherical gravitational wave metrics which \
brings out the power in\nidentification with warp and leads to the simplest \
derivation of exact\nsolutions. These solutions of the Einstein vacuum field \
equations are obtained\nby cutting Minkowski space into two pieces along a \
null cone and re-identifying\nthem with warp which is given by an arbitrary \
non-linear holomorphic\ntransformation. Using 2-component spinor techniques \
we construct a new metric\ndescribing an impulsive spherical gravitational \
wave where the vertex of the\nnull cone lies on a world-line with constant \
