                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1016/S1384-1076(01)00044-6\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"IAA00_25\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Multicolor photometric observations of a planetary \
transit in the system HD\\n209458 are analyzed. The observations, made in the \
Stromgren photometric\\nsystem, allowed a recalculation of the basic physical \
properties of the\\nstar-planet system. This includes derivation of linear \
limb-darkening values of\\nHD 209458, which is the first time that a \
limb-darkening sequence has\\nobservationally been determined for a star \
other than the Sun. As the derived\\nphysical properties depend on \
assumptions that are currently known with limited\\nprecision only, scaling \
relations between derived parameters and assumptions\\nare given. The \
observed limb-darkening is in good agreement with theoretical\\npredictions \
from evolutionary stellar models combined with ATLAS model\\natmospheres, \
verifying these models for the temperature (Teff ~ 6000K), surface\\ngravity \
(log g ~ 4.3) and mass (~ 1.2 Msol) of HD 209458.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
