                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph/0409210\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Robert Braun\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Robert Braun (ASTRON)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"HI Imaging the Low Red-shift Cosmic Web\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"4 pages, 2 figures, to appear in \\\"Science with the \
Square Kilometer\\n  Array,\\\" eds. C. Carilli and S. Rawlings, New \
Astronomy Reviews (Elsevier:\\n  Amsterdam)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"New Astron.Rev. 48 (2004) 1271-1274\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/j.newar.2004.09.010\""}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Only in recent years has the realization emerged that \
galaxies do not\\ndominate the universal baryon budget but are merely the \
brightest pearls of an\\nunderlying Cosmic Web. Although the gas in these \
inter-galactic filaments is\\nmoderately to highly ionized, QSO absorption \
lines have shown that the surface\\narea increases dramatically in going down \
to lower HI column densities. The\\nfirst image of the Cosmic Web in HI \
emission has just been made of the Local\\nGroup filament connecting M31 and \
M33. The corresponding HI distribution\\nfunction is in very good agreement \
with that of the QSO absorption lines,\\nconfirming the 30-fold increase in \
surface area expected between 10^19 cm^-2\\nand 10^17 cm^-2. The critical \
observational challenge is crossing the \\\"HI\\ndesert\\\", the range of \
log(N_HI) from about 19.5 down to 18, over which\\nphoto-ionization by the \
intergalactic radiation field produces an exponential\\ndecline in the \
neutral fraction from essentially unity down to a few percent.\\nNature is \
kinder again to the HI observer below log(N_HI)=18, where the \
neutral\\nfraction decreases only very slowly with log(N_HI). With the SKA we \
can begin\\nthe systematic study of the Cosmic Web beyond the Local Group. \
With moderate\\nintegration times, the necessary resolution and sensitivity \
can be achieved out\\nto distances beyond the Virgo cluster. When combined \
with targeted optical and\\nUV absorption line observations, the total \
baryonic masses and enrichment\\nhistories of the Cosmic Web will be \
determined over the complete range of\\nenvironmental \
over-densities.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 9 Sep 2004 06:50:39 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-10\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"Braun\"", ",", "\"Robert\"", ",", "\"\"", ",", 
                    "\"ASTRON\""}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, 
              ColumnAlignments -> Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
            Function[BoxForm`e$, 
             TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "astro-ph/0409210", "submitter" -> "Robert Braun", 
             "authors" -> "Robert Braun (ASTRON)", "title" -> 
             "HI Imaging the Low Red-shift Cosmic Web", "comments" -> 
             "4 pages, 2 figures, to appear in \"Science with the Square \
Kilometer\n  Array,\" eds. C. Carilli and S. Rawlings, New Astronomy Reviews \
(Elsevier:\n  Amsterdam)", "journal-ref" -> 
             "New Astron.Rev. 48 (2004) 1271-1274", "doi" -> 
             "10.1016/j.newar.2004.09.010", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "astro-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  Only in recent years has the realization emerged that \
galaxies do not\ndominate the universal baryon budget but are merely the \
brightest pearls of an\nunderlying Cosmic Web. Although the gas in these \
inter-galactic filaments is\nmoderately to highly ionized, QSO absorption \
lines have shown that the surface\narea increases dramatically in going down \
to lower HI column densities. The\nfirst image of the Cosmic Web in HI \
emission has just been made of the Local\nGroup filament connecting M31 and \
M33. The corresponding HI distribution\nfunction is in very good agreement \
with that of the QSO absorption lines,\nconfirming the 30-fold increase in \
surface area expected between 10^19 cm^-2\nand 10^17 cm^-2. The critical \
observational challenge is crossing the \"HI\ndesert\", the range of \
log(N_HI) from about 19.5 down to 18, over which\nphoto-ionization by the \
intergalactic radiation field produces an exponential\ndecline in the neutral \
fraction from essentially unity down to a few percent.\nNature is kinder \
again to the HI observer below log(N_HI)=18, where the neutral\nfraction \
decreases only very slowly with log(N_HI). With the SKA we can begin\nthe \
systematic study of the Cosmic Web beyond the Local Group. With moderate\n\
integration times, the necessary resolution and sensitivity can be achieved \
out\nto distances beyond the Virgo cluster. When combined with targeted \
optical and\nUV absorption line observations, the total baryonic masses and \
enrichment\nhistories of the Cosmic Web will be determined over the complete \
range of\nenvironmental over-densities.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Thu, 9 Sep 2004 06:50:39 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2009-11-10", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Braun", "Robert", "", "ASTRON"}}}], 
