                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph/9902221\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Pablo Reig\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Pablo Reig and Paul Roche\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Discovery of two new persistent Be/X-ray pulsar \
systems\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"8 pages 7 figures, accepted for publication in \
MNRAS\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1046/j.1365-8711.1999.02473.x\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"astro-ph\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We present RXTE observations of two recently \
identified massive X-ray\\nbinaries. RX J0440.9+4431/BSD 24-491 and RX \
J1037.5-564/LS 1698 are confirmed\\nas accreting Be/X-ray systems following \
the discovery of X-ray pulsations, with\\nbarycentric pulse periods of 202.5$\
\\\\pm$0.5 s and 860$\\\\pm$2 s respectively. The\\nX-ray spectral analysis \
shows that the energy spectra of the pulsars can be\\nrepresented by a \
power-law, modified at low energy by an absorption component\\nand at high \
energy by a cut-off. Very weak Fe lines may be present. Both\\nsources appear \
to display a low cut-off energy when compared to typical X-ray\\npulsars, low \
X-ray variability (factor of < 10), and no dependence of the X-ray\\nspectrum \
with energy. Given the similarity of these X-ray properties with those\\nof \
the other persistent BeXRB pulsars, 4U0352+309/X Per and RX \
J0146.9+6121/LS\\nI +61 235, we suggest that RX J0440.9+4431/BSD 24-491 and \
RX J1037.5-564/LS\\n1698 are also members of this subclass.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 16 Feb 1999 08:48:56 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
