             "categories" -> "astro-ph", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  We present RXTE observations of two recently identified \
massive X-ray\nbinaries. RX J0440.9+4431/BSD 24-491 and RX J1037.5-564/LS \
1698 are confirmed\nas accreting Be/X-ray systems following the discovery of \
X-ray pulsations, with\nbarycentric pulse periods of 202.5$\\pm$0.5 s and \
860$\\pm$2 s respectively. The\nX-ray spectral analysis shows that the energy \
spectra of the pulsars can be\nrepresented by a power-law, modified at low \
energy by an absorption component\nand at high energy by a cut-off. Very weak \
Fe lines may be present. Both\nsources appear to display a low cut-off energy \
when compared to typical X-ray\npulsars, low X-ray variability (factor of < \
10), and no dependence of the X-ray\nspectrum with energy. Given the \
similarity of these X-ray properties with those\nof the other persistent \
BeXRB pulsars, 4U0352+309/X Per and RX J0146.9+6121/LS\nI +61 235, we suggest \
that RX J0440.9+4431/BSD 24-491 and RX J1037.5-564/LS\n1698 are also members \
of this subclass.\n", 
