                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  It is shown that the precession of a gyroscope can be \
used to elucidate the\\nnature of the smoothness of the null infinity of an \
asymptotically flat\\nspacetime (describing an isolated body). A model for \
which the effects of\\nprecession in the non-smooth null infinity case are of \
order $r^{-2}\\\\ln r$ is\\nproposed. By contrast, in the smooth version the \
effects are of order $r^{-3}$.\\nThis difference should provide an effective \
criterion to decide on the nature\\nof the smoothness of null \
infinity.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
