                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Optical conductivity of a quantum electron gas in a \
Sierpinski carpet\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"6 pages, 9 figures\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys. Rev. B 96, 235438 (2017)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevB.96.235438\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cond-mat.mes-hall\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Recent advances in nanofabrication methods have made \
it possible to create\\ncomplex two-dimensional artificial structures, such \
as fractals, where\\nelectrons can be confined. The optoelectronic and \
plasmonic properties of these\\nexotic quantum electron systems are largely \
unexplored. In this article, we\\ncalculate the optical conductivity of a \
two-dimensional electron gas in a\\nSierpinski carpet (SC). The SC is a \
paradigmatic fractal that can be fabricated\\nin a planar solid-state matrix \
by means of an iterative procedure. We show that\\nthe optical conductivity \
as a function of frequency (i.e. the optical spectrum)\\nconverges, at finite \
temperature, as a function of the fractal iteration. The\\ncalculated optical \
spectrum features sharp peaks at frequencies determined by\\nthe smallest \
geometric details at a given fractal iteration. Each peak is due\\nto \
excitations within sets of electronic state-pairs, whose wave functions \
are\\ncharacterized by quantum confinement in the SC at specific length \
scales,\\nrelated to the frequency of the peak.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 7 Nov 2017 09:37:48 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2018-01-03\""}]}, {
