                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1003.0967\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Tim Byrnes\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Tim Byrnes, Patrik Recher, and Yoshihisa Yamamoto\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Mott transitions of exciton-polaritons and indirect \
excitons in a\\n  periodic potential\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"30 pages, 8 figures\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys. Rev. B 81, 205312 (2010)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevB.81.205312\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"cond-mat.mes-hall cond-mat.other\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We derive an effective Bose-Hubbard model that \
predicts a phase transition\\nfrom Bose-Einstein condensate to Mott insulator \
in two different systems\\nsubject to applied periodic potentials: \
microcavity exciton-polaritons and\\nindirect excitons. Starting from a \
microscopic Hamiltonian of electrons and\\nholes, we derive an effective \
Bose-Hubbard model for both systems and evaluate\\nthe on-site Coulomb \
interaction U and hopping transition amplitudes t.\\nExperimental parameters \
required for observing a phase transition between a\\nBose-Einstein \
condensate and a Mott insulator are discussed. Our results\\nsuggest that \
strong periodic potentials and polaritons with a very large\\nexcitonic \
component are required for observing the phase transition. The form\\nof the \
indirect exciton interaction is derived including direct and \
exchange\\ncomponents of the Coulomb interaction. For indirect excitons, the \
system\\ncrosses over from a Bose-Hubbard model into a double layer \
Fermi-Hubbard model\\nas a function of increasing bilayer separation. The \
Fermi-Hubbard model\\nparameters are calculated, and the criteria for the \
location of this crossover\\nare derived. We conjecture that a crossover \
between a Bose Mott insulator to a\\nFermi Mott insulator should occur with \
increasing bilayer separation.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 4 Mar 2010 05:16:17 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
