Hall-resistivity measurements of MnSi reveal\nthat, although the metastable \
SkL is short-lived at high temperatures, the\nlifetime becomes prolonged (>> \
1 week) at low temperatures. The manipulation of\na delicate balance between \
thermal agitation and the topological stability\nenables a deterministic \
