                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1808.07995\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Changwei Wu\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Chang-Wei Wu, Jun-Han Huang, Dao-Xin Yao\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Tunable room-temperature ferromagnetism in the SiC \
monolayer\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"J. Magn. Magn. Mater. 469, 306 (2019)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/j.jmmm.2018.08.054\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cond-mat.mes-hall\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  It is essential to explore two-dimensional (2D) \
material with magnetic\\nordering in new generation spintronic devices. \
Particularly, the seeking of\\nroom-temperature 2D ferromagnetic (FM) \
materials is a hot topic of current\\nresearch. Here, we study magnetism of \
the Mn-doped and electron-doped SiC\\nmonolayer using first-principle \
calculations. For the Mn-doped SiC monolayer,\\nwe find that either electron \
or hole could mediate the ferromagnetism in the\\nsystem and the Curie \
temperature ($T_C$) can be improved by appropriate carrier\\ndoping. The \
codoping strategy is also discussed on improving $T_C$. The\\ntransition \
between antiferromagnetic and FM phase can be found by strain\\nengineering. \
The $T_C$ is improved above room temperature (RT) under the strain\\nlarger \
than $0.06$. Moreover, the Mn-doped SiC monolayer develops half-metal \
at\\nthe strain range of $0.05-0.1$. On the other hand, the direct electron \
doping\\ncan induce ferromagnetism due to the van Hove singularity in density \
of states\\nof the conduction band edge of the SiC monolayer. The $T_C$ is \
found to be\\naround RT. These fascinating controllable electronic and \
magnetic properties\\nare desired for spintronic applications.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
