Dai, B. Andrei\\n  Bernevig, Zhong Fang, and Zhijun Wang\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Majorana corner modes in unconventional monolayers of \
the 1T-PtSe2\\n  family\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys. Rev. B 110, 035151 (2024)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevB.110.035151\""}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"cond-mat.mtrl-sci cond-mat.supr-con\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In this work, we propose that Majorana zero modes can \
be realized at the\\ncorners of the two-dimensional unconventional insulator. \
We demonstrate that\\n1T-PtSe2 is a symmetry indicator-free (SI-free) \
unconventional insulator,\\noriginating from orbital hybridization between Pt \
$d$ and Se $p_{x,y}$ states.\\nThe kind of SI-free unconventionality has no \
symmetry eigenvalue indication.\\nInstead, it is diagnosed directly by the \
Wannier charge centers by using the\\none-dimensional Wilson loop method. The \
obstructed edge states exhibit strong\\nanisotropy and large Rashba \
splitting. By introducing superconducting proximity\\nand an external \
magnetic field, the Majorana corner modes can be obtained in\\nthe 1T-PtSe2 \
monolayer. In the end, we construct a two-Bernevig-Hughes-Zhang\\nmodel with \
anisotropy to capture the Majorana physics.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
