             "  In this work, we propose that Majorana zero modes can be \
realized at the\ncorners of the two-dimensional unconventional insulator. We \
demonstrate that\n1T-PtSe2 is a symmetry indicator-free (SI-free) \
unconventional insulator,\noriginating from orbital hybridization between Pt \
$d$ and Se $p_{x,y}$ states.\nThe kind of SI-free unconventionality has no \
symmetry eigenvalue indication.\nInstead, it is diagnosed directly by the \
Wannier charge centers by using the\none-dimensional Wilson loop method. The \
obstructed edge states exhibit strong\nanisotropy and large Rashba splitting. \
By introducing superconducting proximity\nand an external magnetic field, the \
Majorana corner modes can be obtained in\nthe 1T-PtSe2 monolayer. In the end, \
we construct a two-Bernevig-Hughes-Zhang\nmodel with anisotropy to capture \
the Majorana physics.\n", 
