             "  Mapping the magnetic exchange interactions from model \
Hamiltonian to density\nfunctional theory is a crucial step in multi-scale \
modeling calculations.\nConsidering the usual magnetic force theorem but with \
arbitrary rotational\nangles of the spin moments, a spurious anisotropy in \
the standard mapping\nprocedure is shown to occur provided by bilinear-like \
contributions of high\norder spin interactions. The evaluation of this \
anisotropy gives a hint on the\nstrength of non-bilinear terms characterizing \
the system under investigation.\n", 
