                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Vasilis Oikonomou\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"V.K. Oikonomou, N. D. Tracas\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Slab Bag Fermionic Casimir effect, Chiral Boundaries and \
Vector Boson -\\n  Majorana Fermion Pistons\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"20 pages, 2 figures\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Int.J.Mod.Phys.A25:5935-5950,2010\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1142/S0217751X10051189\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In this article we consider the Casimir energy and \
force of massless Majorana\\nfermions and vector bosons between parallel \
plates. The vector bosons satisfy\\nperfect electric conductor boundary \
conditions while the Majorana fermions\\nsatisfy bag and chiral boundary \
conditions. We consider various piston\\nconfigurations containing one vector \
boson and one fermion. We present a new\\nregularization mechanism the piston \
offers. In our case regularization occurs\\nexplicitly at the Casimir energy \
density and not at the Casimir force level, as\\nin usual pistons. We make \
use of boundary broken supersymmetry to explain the\\nnumber of fields that \
appear in all the studied cases. The effect of chiral\\nboundary conditions \
in a fermion boson system is investigated. Concerning the\\nsupersymmetry \
issue and the vanishing Casimir energy, we study a massive \
Dirac\\nfermion-scalar boson system with bag and specific Robin type boundary\
\\nconditions for which the Casimir energy vanishes. Finally a two scalar \
bosons\\nsystem between parallel plates is presented in which the \
singularities vanish\\nin the total Casimir energy. A discussion on boundary \
broken supersymmetry\\nfollows.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
