            "id" -> "0912.4825", "submitter" -> "Vasilis Oikonomou", 
             "authors" -> "V.K. Oikonomou, N. D. Tracas", "title" -> 
             "Slab Bag Fermionic Casimir effect, Chiral Boundaries and Vector \
Boson -\n  Majorana Fermion Pistons", "comments" -> "20 pages, 2 figures", 
             "journal-ref" -> "Int.J.Mod.Phys.A25:5935-5950,2010", "doi" -> 
             "10.1142/S0217751X10051189", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  In this article we consider the Casimir energy and force of \
massless Majorana\nfermions and vector bosons between parallel plates. The \
vector bosons satisfy\nperfect electric conductor boundary conditions while \
the Majorana fermions\nsatisfy bag and chiral boundary conditions. We \
consider various piston\nconfigurations containing one vector boson and one \
fermion. We present a new\nregularization mechanism the piston offers. In our \
case regularization occurs\nexplicitly at the Casimir energy density and not \
at the Casimir force level, as\nin usual pistons. We make use of boundary \
broken supersymmetry to explain the\nnumber of fields that appear in all the \
studied cases. The effect of chiral\nboundary conditions in a fermion boson \
system is investigated. Concerning the\nsupersymmetry issue and the vanishing \
Casimir energy, we study a massive Dirac\nfermion-scalar boson system with \
bag and specific Robin type boundary\nconditions for which the Casimir energy \
vanishes. Finally a two scalar bosons\nsystem between parallel plates is \
presented in which the singularities vanish\nin the total Casimir energy. A \
discussion on boundary broken supersymmetry\nfollows.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
