                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1603.05228\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Eugenio R. Bezerra de Mello\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"S. Bellucci, E. R. Bezerra de Mello, E. Bragan\\\\c{c}a \
and A. A.\\n  Saharian\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Finite temperature fermion condensate, charge and \
current densities in a\\n  (2+1)-dimensional conical space\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"30 pages and 9 figures\""}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1140/epjc/s10052-016-4195-5\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We evaluate the fermion condensate and the expectation \
values of the charge\\nand current densities for a massive fermionic field in \
(2+1)-dimensional\\nconical spacetime with a magnetic flux located at the \
cone apex. The\\nconsideration is done for both irreducible representations \
of the Clifford\\nalgebra. The expectation values are decomposed into the \
vacuum expectation\\nvalues and contributions coming from particles and \
antiparticles. All these\\ncontributions are periodic functions of the \
magnetic flux with the period equal\\nto the flux quantum. Related to the \
non-invariance of the model under the\\nparity and time-reversal \
transformations, the fermion condensate and the charge\\ndensity have \
indefinite parity with respect to the change of the signs of the\\nmagnetic \
flux and chemical potential. The expectation value of the radial\\ncurrent \
density vanishes. The azimuthal current density is the same for both\\nthe \
irreducible representations of the Clifford algebra. It is an odd \
function\\nof the magnetic flux and an even function of the chemical \
potential. The\\nbehavior of the expectation values in various asymptotic \
regions of the\\nparameters are discussed in detail. In particular, we show \
that for points near\\nthe cone apex the vacuum parts dominate. For a \
massless field with zero\\nchemical potential the fermion condensate and \
charge density vanish. Simple\\nexpressions are derived for the part in the \
total charge induced by the planar\\nangle deficit and magnetic flux. \
Combining the results for separate irreducible\\nrepresentations, we also \
consider the fermion condensate, charge and current\\ndensities in parity and \
time-reversal symmetric models. Possible applications\\nto graphitic \
nanocones are discussed.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
