\n  Saharian", "title" -> 
             "Finite temperature fermion condensate, charge and current \
densities in a\n  (2+1)-dimensional conical space", "comments" -> 
             "30 pages and 9 figures", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1140/epjc/s10052-016-4195-5", "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "hep-th gr-qc", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We evaluate the fermion condensate and the expectation values \
of the charge\nand current densities for a massive fermionic field in \
(2+1)-dimensional\nconical spacetime with a magnetic flux located at the cone \
apex. The\nconsideration is done for both irreducible representations of the \
Clifford\nalgebra. The expectation values are decomposed into the vacuum \
expectation\nvalues and contributions coming from particles and \
antiparticles. All these\ncontributions are periodic functions of the \
magnetic flux with the period equal\nto the flux quantum. Related to the \
non-invariance of the model under the\nparity and time-reversal \
transformations, the fermion condensate and the charge\ndensity have \
indefinite parity with respect to the change of the signs of the\nmagnetic \
flux and chemical potential. The expectation value of the radial\ncurrent \
density vanishes. The azimuthal current density is the same for both\nthe \
irreducible representations of the Clifford algebra. It is an odd function\n\
of the magnetic flux and an even function of the chemical potential. The\n\
behavior of the expectation values in various asymptotic regions of the\n\
parameters are discussed in detail. In particular, we show that for points \
near\nthe cone apex the vacuum parts dominate. For a massless field with zero\
\nchemical potential the fermion condensate and charge density vanish. Simple\
\nexpressions are derived for the part in the total charge induced by the \
planar\nangle deficit and magnetic flux. Combining the results for separate \
irreducible\nrepresentations, we also consider the fermion condensate, charge \
and current\ndensities in parity and time-reversal symmetric models. Possible \
applications\nto graphitic nanocones are discussed.\n", 
