                  "\"Hyma H. Vallabhapurapu, James P. Slack-Smith, Vikas K. \
Sewani, Chris\\n  Adambukulam, Andrea Morello, Jarryd J. Pla, Arne \
Laucht\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Fast coherent control of an NV- spin ensemble using a \
KTaO3 dielectric\\n  resonator at cryogenic temperatures\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1103/PhysRevApplied.16.044051\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"quant-ph cond-mat.mes-hall\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Microwave delivery to samples in a cryogenic \
environment can pose\\nexperimental challenges such as restricting optical \
access, space constraints\\nand heat generation. Moreover, existing solutions \
that overcome various\\nexperimental restrictions do not necessarily provide \
a large, homogeneous\\noscillating magnetic field over macroscopic \
lengthscales, which is required for\\ncontrol of spin ensembles or fast gate \
operations in scaled-up quantum\\ncomputing implementations. Here we show \
fast and coherent control of a\\nnegatively charged nitrogen vacancy spin \
ensemble by taking advantage of the\\nhigh permittivity of a KTaO3 dielectric \
resonator at cryogenic temperatures. We\\nachieve Rabi frequencies of up to \
48 MHz, with the total field-to-power\\nconversion ratio $C_{\\\\rm P} = $ \
9.66 mT/$\\\\sqrt{\\\\rm W}$ ($\\\\approx191$\\nMHz/$\\\\sqrt{\\\\rm W}$). We \
use the nitrogen vacancy center spin ensemble to probe\\nthe quality factor, \
the coherent enhancement, and the spatial distribution of\\nthe magnetic \
field inside the diamond sample. The key advantages of the\\ndielectric \
resonator utilised in this work are: ease of assembly, in-situ\\ntuneability, \
a high magnetic field conversion efficiency, a low volume\\nfootprint, and \
optical transparency. This makes KTaO3 dielectric resonators a\\npromising \
platform for the delivery of microwave fields for the control of\\nspins in \
various materials at cryogenic temperatures.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
