           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "0805.1221", "submitter" -> "Luis Bonilla L.", "authors" -> 
             "L.L. Bonilla, A. Carpio and I. Plans", "title" -> 
             "Dislocations in cubic crystals described by discrete models", 
             "comments" -> "26 pages, 4 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
             "Physica A 376, 361-377 (2007)", "doi" -> 
             "10.1016/j.physa.2006.10.082", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "cond-mat.mtrl-sci", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  Discrete models of dislocations in cubic crystal lattices \
having one or two\natoms per unit cell are proposed. These models have the \
standard linear\nanisotropic elasticity as their continuum limit and their \
main ingredients are\nthe elastic stiffness constants of the material and a \
dimensionless periodic\nfunction that restores the translation invariance of \
the crystal and influences\nthe dislocation size. For these models, \
conservative and damped equations of\nmotion are proposed. In the latter \
case, the entropy production and\nthermodynamic forces are calculated and \
fluctuation terms obeying the\nfluctuation-dissipation theorem are added. \
Numerical simulations illustrate\nstatic perfect screw and 60$^\\circ$ \
dislocations for GaAs and Si.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
