                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Sergei V. Kalinin, Brian J. Rodriguez, Seung-Hyun Kim, \
S-K. Hong,\\n  Alexei Gruverman and Eugene A. Eliseev\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Imaging Mechanism of Piezoresponse Force Microscopy in \
Capacitor\\n  Structures\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"20 pages, 3 figures, 2 tables, 1 Aappendix, to be \
submitted to Appl.\\n  Phys. Lett\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1063/1.2905266\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cond-mat.mtrl-sci\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The image formation mechanism in Piezoresponse Force \
Microscopy (PFM) of\\ncapacitor structures is analyzed. We demonstrate that \
the spatial resolution is\\na bilinear function of film and top electrode \
thicknesses, and derive the\\ncorresponding analytical expressions. For many \
perovskites, the opposite\\ncontributions of d31 and d33 components can \
result in anomalous domain wall\\nprofiles. This analysis establishes the \
applicability limits of PFM for\\npolarization dynamics studies in \
capacitors, and applies to other structural\\nprobes, including focused X-ray \
studies of capacitor structures.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
