             "abstract" -> 
             "  We report an exact analytical solution of so-called positron \
diffusion\ntrapping model. This model have been widely used for the treatment \
of the\nexperimental data for defect profiling of the adjoin surface layer \
using the\nvariable energy positron (VEP) beam technique. Hovewer, up to now \
this model\ncould be treated only numerically with so-called VEPFIT program. \
The explicit\nform of the solutions is obtained for the realistic cases when \
defect profile\nis described by a discreet step-like function and continuous \
exponential-like\nfunction. Our solutions allow to derive the analytical \
expressions for typical\npositron annihilation characteristics including the \
positron lifetime spectrum.\nLatter quantity could be measured using the \
pulsed, slow positron beam. Our\nanalytical results are in good coincidence \
with both the VEPFIT numerics and\nexperimental data. The presented solutions \
are easily generalizable for defect\nprofiles of other shapes and can be well \
used for much more precise treatment\nof above experimental data.\n", 
