            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1202.0376\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Liang Cui\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Liang Cui, Xiaoying Li and Ningbo Zhao\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Spectral properties of photon pairs generated by \
spontaneous four wave\\n  mixing in inhomogeneous photonic crystal \
fibers\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"to appear in Phys. Rev. A\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevA.85.023825\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"quant-ph physics.optics\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The photonic crystal fiber (PCF) is one of the \
excellent media for generating\\nphoton pairs via spontaneous four wave \
mixing. Here we study how the\\ninhomogeneity of PCFs affect the spectral \
properties of photon pairs from both\\nthe theoretical and experimental \
aspects. The theoretical model shows that the\\nphoton pairs born in \
different place of the inhomogeneous PCF are coherently\\nsuperposed, and a \
modulation in the broadened spectrum of phase matching\\nfunction will \
appear, which prevents the realization of spectral factorable\\nphoton pairs. \
In particular, the inhomogeneity induced modulation can be\\nexamined by \
measuring the spectrum of individual signal or idler field when \
the\\nasymmetric group velocity matching is approximately fulfilled. Our \
experiments\\nare performed by tailoring the spectrum of pulsed pump to \
satisfy the specified\\nphase matching condition. The observed spectra of \
individual signal photons,\\nwhich are produced from different segments of \
the 1.9 m inhomogeneous PCF,\\nagree with the theoretical predictions. The \
investigations are not only useful\\nfor fiber based quantum state \
engineering, but also provide a dependable method\\nto test the homogeneity \
of PCF.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
