             "Spectral properties of photon pairs generated by spontaneous \
four wave\n  mixing in inhomogeneous photonic crystal fibers", "comments" -> 
             "to appear in Phys. Rev. A", "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1103/PhysRevA.85.023825", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "quant-ph physics.optics", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  The photonic crystal fiber (PCF) is one of the excellent \
media for generating\nphoton pairs via spontaneous four wave mixing. Here we \
study how the\ninhomogeneity of PCFs affect the spectral properties of photon \
pairs from both\nthe theoretical and experimental aspects. The theoretical \
model shows that the\nphoton pairs born in different place of the \
inhomogeneous PCF are coherently\nsuperposed, and a modulation in the \
broadened spectrum of phase matching\nfunction will appear, which prevents \
the realization of spectral factorable\nphoton pairs. In particular, the \
inhomogeneity induced modulation can be\nexamined by measuring the spectrum \
of individual signal or idler field when the\nasymmetric group velocity \
matching is approximately fulfilled. Our experiments\nare performed by \
tailoring the spectrum of pulsed pump to satisfy the specified\nphase \
matching condition. The observed spectra of individual signal photons,\nwhich \
are produced from different segments of the 1.9 m inhomogeneous PCF,\nagree \
with the theoretical predictions. The investigations are not only useful\nfor \
fiber based quantum state engineering, but also provide a dependable method\n\
to test the homogeneity of PCF.\n", 
