particular class of\nquantum algorithms, called graph algorithms, which \
correspond in the binary\ncase to the Clifford group part of a network and \
which can efficiently be\nimplemented on a one-way quantum computer. These \
algorithms can ``completely be\nsolved\" in the sense that the manipulation \
of quantum states in each step can\nbe computed explicitly. Graph algorithms \
are precisely those which implement\nencoding schemes for graph codes. \
