                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We present a method of directly obtaining the parity \
of a Gaussian state of\\nlight without recourse to photon-number counting. \
The scheme uses only a simple\\nbalanced homodyne technique, and intensity \
correlation. Thus interferometric\\nschemes utilizing coherent or squeezed \
light, and parity detection may be\\npractically implemented for an arbitrary \
photon flux. Specifically we\\ninvestigate a two-mode, squeezed-light, \
Mach-Zehnder interferometer and show\\nhow the parity of the output state may \
be obtained. We also show that the\\ndetection may be described independent \
of the parity operator, and that this\\n\\\"parity-by-proxy\\\" measurement \
has the same signal as traditional parity.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
