                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2312.00960\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Satya Sai Srinath Namburi\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Satya Sai Srinath Namburi, Makesh Sreedhar, Srinath \
Srinivasan,\\n  Frederic Sala\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"The Cost of Compression: Investigating the Impact of \
Compression on\\n  Parametric Knowledge in Language Models\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Accepted to EMNLP 2023 Findings\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cs.CL cs.AI cs.LG\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Compressing large language models (LLMs), often \
consisting of billions of\\nparameters, provides faster inference, smaller \
memory footprints, and enables\\nlocal deployment. Two standard compression \
techniques are pruning and\\nquantization, with the former eliminating \
redundant connections in model layers\\nand the latter representing model \
parameters with fewer bits. The key tradeoff\\nis between the degree of \
compression and the impact on the quality of the\\ncompressed model. Existing \
research on LLM compression primarily focuses on\\nperformance in terms of \
general metrics like perplexity or downstream task\\naccuracy. More \
fine-grained metrics, such as those measuring parametric\\nknowledge, remain \
significantly underexplored. To help bridge this gap, we\\npresent a \
comprehensive analysis across multiple model families \
(ENCODER,\\nENCODER-DECODER, and DECODER) using the LAMA and LM-HARNESS \
benchmarks in order\\nto systematically quantify the effect of commonly \
employed compression\\ntechniques on model performance. A particular focus is \
on tradeoffs involving\\nparametric knowledge, with the goal of providing \
practitioners with practical\\ninsights to help make informed decisions on \
compression. We release our\\ncodebase1 to enable further research.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 1 Dec 2023 22:27:12 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2023-12-05\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
