           DiskBox[{3.864108121579384, -15.423503511747802`}, 
            0.12358081394744114],
           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1904.07850\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Xingyi Zhou\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Xingyi Zhou, Dequan Wang, Philipp \
Kr\\\\\\\"ahenb\\\\\\\"uhl\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"title\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Objects as Points\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"12 pages, 5 figures\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cs.CV\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Detection identifies objects as axis-aligned boxes in \
an image. Most\\nsuccessful object detectors enumerate a nearly exhaustive \
list of potential\\nobject locations and classify each. This is wasteful, \
inefficient, and requires\\nadditional post-processing. In this paper, we \
take a different approach. We\\nmodel an object as a single point --- the \
center point of its bounding box. Our\\ndetector uses keypoint estimation to \
find center points and regresses to all\\nother object properties, such as \
size, 3D location, orientation, and even pose.\\nOur center point based \
approach, CenterNet, is end-to-end differentiable,\\nsimpler, faster, and \
more accurate than corresponding bounding box based\\ndetectors. CenterNet \
achieves the best speed-accuracy trade-off on the MS COCO\\ndataset, with \
28.1% AP at 142 FPS, 37.4% AP at 52 FPS, and 45.1% AP with\\nmulti-scale \
testing at 1.4 FPS. We use the same approach to estimate 3D\\nbounding box in \
the KITTI benchmark and human pose on the COCO keypoint\\ndataset. Our method \
performs competitively with sophisticated multi-stage\\nmethods and runs in \
real-time.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 16 Apr 2019 17:54:26 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
