                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2311.05669\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Yuqi Hou\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Yuqi Hou, Zhongqun Zhang, Nora Horanyi, Jaewon Moon, \
Yihua Cheng,\\n  Hyung Jin Chang\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Multi-Modal Gaze Following in Conversational \
Scenarios\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cs.CV\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Gaze following estimates gaze targets of in-scene \
person by understanding\\nhuman behavior and scene information. Existing \
methods usually analyze scene\\nimages for gaze following. However, compared \
with visual images, audio also\\nprovides crucial cues for determining human \
behavior.This suggests that we can\\nfurther improve gaze following \
considering audio cues. In this paper, we\\nexplore gaze following tasks in \
conversational scenarios. We propose a novel\\nmulti-modal gaze following \
framework based on our observation ``audiences tend\\nto focus on the \
speaker''. We first leverage the correlation between audio and\\nlips, and \
classify speakers and listeners in a scene. We then use the \
identity\\ninformation to enhance scene images and propose a gaze candidate \
estimation\\nnetwork. The network estimates gaze candidates from enhanced \
scene images and\\nwe use MLP to match subjects with candidates as \
classification tasks. Existing\\ngaze following datasets focus on visual \
images while ignore audios.To evaluate\\nour method, we collect a \
conversational dataset, VideoGazeSpeech (VGS), which\\nis the first gaze \
following dataset including images and audio. Our method\\nsignificantly \
outperforms existing methods in VGS datasets. The visualization\\nresult also \
prove the advantage of audio cues in gaze following tasks. Our work\\nwill \
inspire more researches in multi-modal gaze following estimation.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
