           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2301.04805\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Zixuan Chen\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Zixuan Chen, Zewei He, Zhe-Ming Lu\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"DEA-Net: Single image dehazing based on detail-enhanced \
convolution and\\n  content-guided attention\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"cs.CV\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  
                  "\"  Single image dehazing is a challenging ill-posed \
problem which estimates\\nlatent haze-free images from observed hazy images. \
Some existing deep learning\\nbased methods are devoted to improving the \
model performance via increasing the\\ndepth or width of convolution. The \
learning ability of convolutional neural\\nnetwork (CNN) structure is still \
under-explored. In this paper, a\\ndetail-enhanced attention block (DEAB) \
consisting of the detail-enhanced\\nconvolution (DEConv) and the \
content-guided attention (CGA) is proposed to\\nboost the feature learning \
for improving the dehazing performance.\\nSpecifically, the DEConv integrates \
prior information into normal convolution\\nlayer to enhance the \
representation and generalization capacity. Then by using\\nthe \
re-parameterization technique, DEConv is equivalently converted into \
a\\nvanilla convolution with NO extra parameters and computational cost. \
By\\nassigning unique spatial importance map (SIM) to every channel, CGA can \
attend\\nmore useful information encoded in features. In addition, a \
CGA-based mixup\\nfusion scheme is presented to effectively fuse the features \
and aid the\\ngradient flow. By combining above mentioned components, we \
propose our\\ndetail-enhanced attention network (DEA-Net) for recovering \
high-quality\\nhaze-free images. Extensive experimental results demonstrate \
the effectiveness\\nof our DEA-Net, outperforming the state-of-the-art (SOTA) \
methods by boosting\\nthe PSNR index over 41 dB with only 3.653 M parameters. \
The source code of our\\nDEA-Net will be made available at \
https://github.com/cecret3350/DEA-Net.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 12 Jan 2023 04:27:22 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2023-01-13\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Chen\"", ",", "\"Zixuan\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"He\"", ",", "\"Zewei\"", ",", "\"\""}], "}"}], 
                    ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Lu\"", ",", "\"Zhe-Ming\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
              Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
            Function[BoxForm`e$, 
             TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "2301.04805", "submitter" -> "Zixuan Chen", "authors" -> 
             "Zixuan Chen, Zewei He, Zhe-Ming Lu", "title" -> 
             "DEA-Net: Single image dehazing based on detail-enhanced \
convolution and\n  content-guided attention", "comments" -> Null, 
             "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> Null, "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "cs.CV", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  Single image dehazing is a challenging ill-posed problem \
which estimates\nlatent haze-free images from observed hazy images. Some \
existing deep learning\nbased methods are devoted to improving the model \
performance via increasing the\ndepth or width of convolution. The learning \
ability of convolutional neural\nnetwork (CNN) structure is still \
under-explored. In this paper, a\ndetail-enhanced attention block (DEAB) \
consisting of the detail-enhanced\nconvolution (DEConv) and the \
content-guided attention (CGA) is proposed to\nboost the feature learning for \
improving the dehazing performance.\nSpecifically, the DEConv integrates \
prior information into normal convolution\nlayer to enhance the \
representation and generalization capacity. Then by using\nthe \
re-parameterization technique, DEConv is equivalently converted into a\n\
vanilla convolution with NO extra parameters and computational cost. By\n\
assigning unique spatial importance map (SIM) to every channel, CGA can \
attend\nmore useful information encoded in features. In addition, a CGA-based \
mixup\nfusion scheme is presented to effectively fuse the features and aid \
the\ngradient flow. By combining above mentioned components, we propose our\n\
detail-enhanced attention network (DEA-Net) for recovering high-quality\n\
haze-free images. Extensive experimental results demonstrate the \
effectiveness\nof our DEA-Net, outperforming the state-of-the-art (SOTA) \
methods by boosting\nthe PSNR index over 41 dB with only 3.653 M parameters. \
The source code of our\nDEA-Net will be made available at \
https://github.com/cecret3350/DEA-Net.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
