             "  The effective localization of mitosis is a critical \
precursory task for\ndeciding tumor prognosis and grade. Automated mitosis \
detection through deep\nlearning-oriented image analysis often fails on \
unseen patient data due to\ninherent domain biases. This paper proposes a \
domain homogenizer for mitosis\ndetection that attempts to alleviate domain \
differences in histology images via\nadversarial reconstruction of input \
images. The proposed homogenizer is based\non a U-Net architecture and can \
effectively reduce domain differences commonly\nseen with histology imaging \
data. We demonstrate our domain homogenizer's\neffectiveness by observing the \
reduction in domain differences between the\npreprocessed images. Using this \
homogenizer, along with a subsequent retina-net\nobject detector, we were \
able to outperform the baselines of the 2021 MIDOG\nchallenge in terms of \
average precision of the detected mitotic figures.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
