           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "2103.13655", "submitter" -> "Tizian Wenzel", "authors" -> 
             
             "Tizian Wenzel, Marius Kurz, Andrea Beck, Gabriele Santin, \
Bernard\n  Haasdonk", "title" -> 
             "Structured Deep Kernel Networks for Data-Driven Closure Terms \
of\n  Turbulent Flows", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1007/978-3-030-97549-4_47", "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "cs.LG cs.NA math.NA", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  Standard kernel methods for machine learning usually struggle \
when dealing\nwith large datasets. We review a recently introduced Structured \
Deep Kernel\nNetwork (SDKN) approach that is capable of dealing with \
high-dimensional and\nhuge datasets - and enjoys typical standard machine \
learning approximation\nproperties. We extend the SDKN to combine it with \
standard machine learning\nmodules and compare it with Neural Networks on the \
scientific challenge of\ndata-driven prediction of closure terms of turbulent \
flows. We show\nexperimentally that the SDKNs are capable of dealing with \
large datasets and\nachieve near-perfect accuracy on the given application.\n\
", "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Thu, 25 Mar 2021 08:04:35 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2022-10-31", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Wenzel", "Tizian", ""}, {
