                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1206.6296\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Joao Magueijo\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Stephon Alexander, Joao Magueijo and Antonino \
Marciano\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Horava-Lifshitz theory as a Fermionic Aether in Ashtekar \
gravity\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.86.064025\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"hep-th astro-ph.CO gr-qc\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We show how Ho\\\\v{r}ava-Lifshitz (HL) theory appears \
naturally in the Ashtekar\\nformulation of relativity if one postulates the \
existence of a fermionic field\\nplaying the role of aether. The spatial \
currents associated with this field\\nmust be switched off for the \
equivalence to work. Therefore the field supplies\\nthe preferred frame \
associated with breaking refoliation (time diffeomorphism)\\ninvariance, but \
obviously the symmetry is only spontaneously broken if the\\nfield is \
dynamic. When Dirac fermions couple to the gravitational field via \
the\\nAshtekar variables, the low energy limit of HL gravity, recast in the \
language\\nof Ashtekar variables, naturally emerges (provided the spatial \
fermion current\\nidentically vanishes). HL gravity can therefore be \
interpreted as a time-like\\ncurrent, or a Fermi aether, that fills \
space-time, with the Immirzi parameter,\\na chiral fermionic coupling, and \
the fermionic charge density fixing the value\\nof the parameter $\\\\lambda$ \
determining HL theory. This reinterpretation sheds\\nlight on some features \
of HL theory, namely its good convergence properties.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 27 Jun 2012 15:07:14 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2015-06-05\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
