            "id" -> "1206.6296", "submitter" -> "Joao Magueijo", "authors" -> 
             "Stephon Alexander, Joao Magueijo and Antonino Marciano", 
             "title" -> 
             "Horava-Lifshitz theory as a Fermionic Aether in Ashtekar \
gravity", "comments" -> Null, "journal-ref" -> Null, "doi" -> 
             "10.1103/PhysRevD.86.064025", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "hep-th astro-ph.CO gr-qc", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We show how Ho\\v{r}ava-Lifshitz (HL) theory appears \
naturally in the Ashtekar\nformulation of relativity if one postulates the \
existence of a fermionic field\nplaying the role of aether. The spatial \
currents associated with this field\nmust be switched off for the equivalence \
to work. Therefore the field supplies\nthe preferred frame associated with \
breaking refoliation (time diffeomorphism)\ninvariance, but obviously the \
symmetry is only spontaneously broken if the\nfield is dynamic. When Dirac \
fermions couple to the gravitational field via the\nAshtekar variables, the \
low energy limit of HL gravity, recast in the language\nof Ashtekar \
variables, naturally emerges (provided the spatial fermion current\n\
identically vanishes). HL gravity can therefore be interpreted as a time-like\
\ncurrent, or a Fermi aether, that fills space-time, with the Immirzi \
parameter,\na chiral fermionic coupling, and the fermionic charge density \
fixing the value\nof the parameter $\\lambda$ determining HL theory. This \
reinterpretation sheds\nlight on some features of HL theory, namely its good \
convergence properties.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
