                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1708.02373\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Hyeong-Chan Kim\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Hyeong-Chan Kim\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Black hole in closed spacetime with an anisotropic fluid\
\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"15 pages, 7 figures\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys. Rev. D 96, 064053 (2017)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.96.064053\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study spherically symmetric geometries made of \
anisotropic perfect fluid\\nbased on general relativity. The purpose of the \
work is to find and classify\\nblack hole solutions in closed spacetime. In a \
general setting, we find that a\\nstatic and closed space exists only when \
the radial pressure is negative but\\nits size is smaller than the density. \
The Einstein equation is eventually\\ncasted into a first order autonomous \
equation on two-dimensional plane of\\nscale-invariant variables, which are \
equivalent to the\\nTolman-Oppenheimer-Volkoff (TOV) equation in general \
relativity. Then, we\\ndisplay various solution curves numerically. An exact \
solution describing a\\nblack hole solution in a closed spacetime was known \
in Ref. [1], which solution\\nbears a naked singularity and negative energy \
era. We find that the two\\ndeficits can be remedied when $\\\\rho+3p_1>0$ \
and $\\\\rho+p_1+2p_2< 0$, where the\\nsecond violates the strong energy \
condition.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Tue, 8 Aug 2017 05:09:23 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2017-10-04\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Kim\"", ",", "\"Hyeong-Chan\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
              Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
            Function[BoxForm`e$, 
             TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "1708.02373", "submitter" -> "Hyeong-Chan Kim", "authors" -> 
             "Hyeong-Chan Kim", "title" -> 
             "Black hole in closed spacetime with an anisotropic fluid", 
             "comments" -> "15 pages, 7 figures", "journal-ref" -> 
             "Phys. Rev. D 96, 064053 (2017)", "doi" -> 
             "10.1103/PhysRevD.96.064053", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "gr-qc", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We study spherically symmetric geometries made of anisotropic \
perfect fluid\nbased on general relativity. The purpose of the work is to \
find and classify\nblack hole solutions in closed spacetime. In a general \
setting, we find that a\nstatic and closed space exists only when the radial \
pressure is negative but\nits size is smaller than the density. The Einstein \
equation is eventually\ncasted into a first order autonomous equation on \
two-dimensional plane of\nscale-invariant variables, which are equivalent to \
the\nTolman-Oppenheimer-Volkoff (TOV) equation in general relativity. Then, \
we\ndisplay various solution curves numerically. An exact solution describing \
a\nblack hole solution in a closed spacetime was known in Ref. [1], which \
solution\nbears a naked singularity and negative energy era. We find that the \
two\ndeficits can be remedied when $\\rho+3p_1>0$ and $\\rho+p_1+2p_2< 0$, \
where the\nsecond violates the strong energy condition.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Tue, 8 Aug 2017 05:09:23 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2017-10-04", "authors_parsed" -> {{"Kim", "Hyeong-Chan", ""}}}],
