            0.12358081394744114],
           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc/0311064\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"T. Roy Choudhury\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"T. Roy Choudhury, T. Padmanabhan\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Quasi normal modes in Schwarzschild-DeSitter spacetime: \
A simple\\n  derivation of the level spacing of the frequencies\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Revised version. Accepted in Phys. Rev. D\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Rev. D69 (2004) 064033\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.69.064033\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc astro-ph hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  It is known that the imaginary parts of the quasi \
normal mode (QNM)\\nfrequencies for the Schwarzschild black hole are evenly \
spaced with a spacing\\nthat depends only on the surface gravity. On the \
other hand, for massless\\nminimally coupled scalar fields, there exist no \
QNMs in the pure DeSitter\\nspacetime. It is not clear what the structure of \
the QNMs would be for the\\nSchwarzschild-DeSitter (SDS) spacetime, which is \
characterized by two different\\nsurface gravities. We provide a simple \
derivation of the imaginary parts of the\\nQNM frequencies for the SDS \
spacetime by calculating the scattering amplitude\\nin the first Born \
approximation and determining its poles. We find that, for\\nthe usual set of \
boundary conditions in which the incident wave is scattered\\noff the black \
hole horizon, the imaginary parts of the QNM frequencies have a\\nequally \
spaced structure with the level spacing depending on the surface\\ngravity of \
the black hole. Several conceptual issues related to the QNM are\\ndiscussed \
in the light of this result and comparison with previous work is\\npresented.\
\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 20 Nov 2003 09:10:29 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 19 Jan 2004 14:12:16 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                    "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2009-11-10\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Choudhury\"", ",", "\"T. Roy\"", ",", "\"\""}],
