             "  It is known that the imaginary parts of the quasi normal mode \
(QNM)\nfrequencies for the Schwarzschild black hole are evenly spaced with a \
spacing\nthat depends only on the surface gravity. On the other hand, for \
massless\nminimally coupled scalar fields, there exist no QNMs in the pure \
DeSitter\nspacetime. It is not clear what the structure of the QNMs would be \
for the\nSchwarzschild-DeSitter (SDS) spacetime, which is characterized by \
two different\nsurface gravities. We provide a simple derivation of the \
imaginary parts of the\nQNM frequencies for the SDS spacetime by calculating \
the scattering amplitude\nin the first Born approximation and determining its \
poles. We find that, for\nthe usual set of boundary conditions in which the \
incident wave is scattered\noff the black hole horizon, the imaginary parts \
of the QNM frequencies have a\nequally spaced structure with the level \
spacing depending on the surface\ngravity of the black hole. Several \
conceptual issues related to the QNM are\ndiscussed in the light of this \
result and comparison with previous work is\npresented.\n", 
