            "id" -> "gr-qc/0202100", "submitter" -> "Farid Ya. Khalili", 
             "authors" -> "S.L.Danilishin, F.Ya.Khalili", "title" -> 
             "Stroboscopic Variation Measurement", "comments" -> 
             
             "13 pages, 2 figures drawn in TeX and 2 figures in postscript,\n \
 misprint corrected", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Lett. A300 (2002) 547-558", 
             "doi" -> "10.1016/S0375-9601(02)00903-9", "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "gr-qc", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  A new procedure of the linear position measurement which \
allows to obtain\nsensitivity better than the Standard Quantum Limit and \
close to the Energetic\nQuantum Limit is proposed and analyzed in details. \
Proposed method is based on\nthe principles of stroboscopic quantum \
measurement and variation quantum\nmeasurement and allows to avoid main \
disadvantages of both these procedures.\nThis method can be considered as a \
good candidate for use as a local position\nmeter in the ``intracavity'' \
topologies of the laser gravitational-wave\nantennae.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
