                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2310.06142\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jiaxuan Wang\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Jiaxuan Wang, Ruynet. L. de Matos Filho, Girish S. \
Agarwal, and Luiz\\n  Davidovich\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Quantum advantage of time-reversed ancilla-based \
metrology of absorption\\n  parameters\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"14 pages, 7 figures\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1103/PhysRevResearch.6.013034\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys. Rev. Research 6, 013034\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"quant-ph\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Quantum estimation of parameters defining open-system \
dynamics may be\\nenhanced by using ancillas that are entangled with the \
probe but are not\\nsubmitted to the dynamics. Here we consider the important \
problem of estimation\\nof transmission of light by a sample, with losses due \
to absorption and\\nscattering. We show, through the determination of the \
quantum Fisher\\ninformation, that the ancilla strategy leads to the best \
possible precision in\\nsingle-mode estimation, the one obtained for a Fock \
state input, through joint\\nphoton-counting of probe and ancilla, which are \
modes of a bimodal squeezed\\nstate produced by an optical parametric \
amplifier. This proposal overcomes the\\nchallenge of producing and detecting \
high photon-number Fock states, and it is\\nquite robust against additional \
noise: we show that it is immune to phase noise\\nand the precision does not \
change if the incoming state gets disentangled.\\nFurthermore, the quantum \
gain is still present under moderate photon losses of\\nthe input beams. We \
also discuss an alternative to joint photon counting, which\\nis readily \
implementable with present technology, and approaches the quantum\\nFisher \
information result for weak absorption, even with moderate photons\\nlosses \
of the input beams before the sample is probed: a time-reversal\\nprocedure, \
placing the sample between two optical parametric amplifiers, with\\nthe \
second undoing the squeezing produced by the first one. The precision \
of\\nestimation of the loss parameter is obtained from the average outgoing \
total\\nphoton number and its variance. In both procedures, the state of the \
probe and\\nthe detection procedure are independent of the value of the \
parameter.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 9 Oct 2023 20:41:53 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v2\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Wed, 6 Dec 2023 16:05:09 GMT\""}]}], "}"}]}], 
                    "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2024-03-04\""}]}, {
