, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Quantum particles can be obtained from a classical \
probability distribution\\nin phase space by a suitable coarse graining, \
whereby simultaneous classical\\ninformation about position and momentum can \
be lost. For a suitable time\\nevolution of the classical probabilities and \
choice of observables all features\\nof a quantum particle in a potential \
follow from classical statistics. This\\nincludes interference, tunneling and \
the uncertainty relation.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
