                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  MadGraph5_aMC@NLO is a software package that allows \
one to simulate processes\\nof arbitrary complexity, at both the leading and \
the next-to-leading order\\nperturbative accuracy, with or without matching \
and multi-jet merging to parton\\nshowers. It has been designed for, and so \
far primarily employed in the context\\nof, hadronic collisions. In this \
note, we document the implementation of a few\\ntechnical features that are \
necessary to extend its scope to realistic ee\\ncollider environments. We \
limit ourselves to discussing the unpolarized beam\\ncase, but we point out \
that the treatment of polarized beams is conceptually\\nidentical, and that \
the structure we set up can easily be extended to carry out\\nsimulations at \
muon colliders.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Mon, 23 Aug 2021 15:59:04 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2021-08-24\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
