, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In this paper, a study of light-cone distribution \
amplitudes for p-wave heavy\\nmesons is presented in both general and heavy \
quark frameworks. Within the\\nlight-front approach, the leading twist \
light-cone distribution amplitudes,\\n\\\\phi_M(u) and their relevant decay \
constants of heavy scalar, axial-vector and\\ntensor mesons, f_M, are \
formulated. The relations of some decay constants can\\nbe simplified when \
the heavy quark limit is taken into account. After fixing\\nthe parameters \
which appear in a Gaussian wave function, the corresponding\\ndecay constants \
are calculated and compared with those of other theoretical\\napproaches. The \
curves and the first six \\\\xi moments of \\\\phi_M(u) are plotted\\nand \
estimated. These results all endorse the requirements of heavy \
quark\\nsymmetry.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
