                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  A standing problem in neutrino physics is the \
consistent and universal\\ndefinition of oscillating neutrino states as \
coherent superpositions of massive\\nneutrino states. This problem is solved \
in a quantum field theoretical\\nframework of neutrino mixing developed in \
analogy with the Nambu--Jona-Lasinio\\nmodel for the dynamical generation of \
nucleon masses. The massive neutrino\\nstates are Bogoliubov quasiparticles \
and their vacuum is a condensate of\\n\\\"Cooper pairs\\\" of massless \
flavour neutrinos. Their superpositions as\\noscillating neutrino states have \
intrinsic quantum coherence by construction.\\nIn this quantization \
framework, the standard phenomenological flavour neutrino\\nstates and \
oscillation probability formula are validated in the\\nultrarelativistic \
approximation.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
