                  "\"Boundary Conditions in Quantum String Cosmology\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"16 pages, REVTEX, minor changes, two references \
added\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Lett. B397 (1997) 185-192\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1016/S0370-2693(97)00192-5\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Freiburg THEP-96/25\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We discuss in detail how to consistently impose \
boundary conditions in\\nquantum string cosmology. Since a classical time \
parameter is absent in quantum\\ngravity, such conditions must be imposed \
with respect to intrinsic variables.\\nConstructing wave packets for \
minisuperspace models from different tree-level\\nstring effective actions, \
we explain in particular the meaning of a transition\\nbetween ``pre-big-bang\
\\\" and ``post-big-bang\\\" branches. This leads to a scenario\\ndifferent \
from previous considerations.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Thu, 9 Jan 1997 14:03:23 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
