            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2303.13286\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Marina David\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Pablo A. Cano, Marina David\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"The extremal Kerr entropy in higher-derivative gravities\
\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"33 pages+appendices, one figure\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1007/JHEP05(2023)219\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th gr-qc\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We investigate higher derivative corrections to the \
extremal Kerr black hole\\nin the context of heterotic string theory with $\\\
\\alpha'$ corrections and of a\\ncubic-curvature extension of general \
relativity. By analyzing the near-horizon\\nextremal geometry of these black \
holes, we are able to compute the Iyer-Wald\\nentropy as well as the angular \
momentum via generalized Komar integrals. In the\\ncase of the stringy \
corrections, we obtain the physically relevant relation\\n$S(J)$ at order $\\\
\\alpha'^2$. On the other hand, the cubic theories, which are\\nchosen as \
Einsteinian cubic gravity plus a new odd-parity density with\\nanalogous \
features, possess special integrability properties that enable us to\\nobtain \
exact results in the higher-derivative couplings. This allows us to \
find\\nthe relation $S(J)$ at arbitrary orders in the couplings and even to \
study it\\nin a non-perturbative way. We also extend our analysis to the case \
of the\\nextremal Kerr-(A)dS black hole.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
